Directive 2: Contraband Inventory System (C++)
This system manages items that increase your "Heat" level. If you are scanned by a Metal Detector while carrying these, the AI triggers an immediate search.

Core Structure: UContrabandComponent

C++
// UContrabandComponent.h (UE 5.3.2)
USTRUCT(BlueprintType)
struct FContrabandItem {
    GENERATED_BODY()
    UPROPERTY(EditAnywhere) FString ItemName;
    UPROPERTY(EditAnywhere) float HeatValue; // How much this spikes suspicion
    UPROPERTY(EditAnywhere) bool bIsMetallic; // Detected by Sector 1 scanners
};

// Logic for Proximity Scanners
void UContrabandComponent::OnScanned() {
    float TotalHeat = 0.0f;
    for (auto& Item : CurrentInventory) {
        if (Item.bIsMetallic) TotalHeat += Item.HeatValue;
    }
    // Update global BraxtigConfig Heat
    UBraxtigSubsystem::Get()->AddHeat(TotalHeat);
}
Directive 3: "Nightshade" Stealth Mechanics
Stealth in this project is based on Lumen-integrated Light Detection and Audio Occlusion.

The "Gaze" and the "Shadow"
Industrial Hum Cover: Players can sprint without being heard ONLY when the SpinFan assets (at coordinates like 400, 283, 204) are in their "Alert" or "Lockdown" high-RPM cycles. The mechanical whine occludes footsteps.

Visor Ghosting: While in "Mjolnir's Gaze" mode (Purple/Green HLSL), the player moves 20% slower but can see guard "Perception Cones" through the InsideWallDoorWay meshes.

Vent Navigation: The vents (extracted coordinates 400, 283, 204) act as "Zero-Heat" zones. Guards will not enter vents unless the player has reached >90% Heat, at which point the Warden executes a "Vent Purge" (Fan speed 4.0).

