1. Procedural Patrol Mapping (Python)
Action: Scans the 11,269 assets, identifies the floor tile grid (at Y-level -318 for bathrooms and -25 for kitchen), and procedurally spawns TargetPoint actors to create a global AI patrol network.

Python
import unreal

def map_guard_patrols():
    # Identify floor tiles for patrol nodes
    all_actors = unreal.EditorLevelLibrary.get_all_level_actors()
    floor_tiles = [a for a in all_actors if "FloorTile" in a.get_actor_label()]
    
    # Grid sampling (every 50th tile to prevent node overflow)
    patrol_nodes = floor_tiles[::50]
    
    for i, tile in enumerate(patrol_nodes):
        loc = tile.get_actor_location()
        # Raise 50 units off floor
        loc.z += 50.0 
        
        node = unreal.EditorLevelLibrary.spawn_actor_from_class(unreal.TargetPoint, loc)
        node.set_actor_label(f"PatrolNode_Sector_{i}")
        # Tag for AI perception
        node.add_tag("PatrolPoint")

    unreal.log(f"BraxtigConfig: {len(patrol_nodes)} Patrol Nodes generated across the tile grid.")

map_guard_patrols()
2. Nurse Bridget Trauma-Response System (C++ / Logic)
Action: Implements a specialized dialogue component for Bridget Galletti. It calculates "Trauma Triggers" if the player's Heat level is high or if they are injured, switching her persona from "Nurse" to "Artist."

C++
// BridgetLogicComponent.cpp
void UBridgetLogicComponent::OnPlayerProximity(ANyghtshadeCharacter* Player) {
    float Heat = Player->CurrentHeat;
    bool bIsInjured = Player->GetHealth() < 50.0f;

    // Trauma-Response Logic
    if (Heat > 80.0f) {
        // Persona: Artist (Hostile/Clinical)
        TriggerDialogue("BG_HighHeat_Artist");
        SetMjolnirStencil(254); // Glow Purple
    }
    else if (bIsInjured) {
        // Persona: Nurse (Helpful/Noir)
        TriggerDialogue("BG_Injured_Nurse");
        Player->Heal(10.0f);
    }
    else {
        TriggerDialogue("BG_Default_Idle");
    }
}
