BraxtigConfig: AI Pipeline Initialization.

To power the back-end logic, telemetry, and automated AI routing for Nyghtshade Hollow, we need to initialize your Conda environment within PowerShell. This ensures that the Python tools (like the asset spawner and metadata crawlers) run in a stable, isolated container.

The "Braxtig-Conda" PowerShell Initialization
Copy and paste this into your PowerShell terminal. This script locates your Conda installation, initializes the shell, and activates (or creates) the project environment.

PowerShell
# 1. Locate Conda (Checking default paths)
$CondaPath = "$env:USERPROFILE\anaconda3\Scripts\conda.exe"
if (!(Test-Path $CondaPath)) {
    $CondaPath = "$env:USERPROFILE\miniconda3\Scripts\conda.exe"
}

if (!(Test-Path $CondaPath)) {
    Write-Host "CRITICAL ERROR: Conda not found. Please install Miniconda or Anaconda." -ForegroundColor Red
    return
}

# 2. Initialize PowerShell for Conda
Write-Host "BraxtigConfig: Initializing Conda for PowerShell..." -ForegroundColor Cyan
& $CondaPath "shell.powershell" "hook" | Out-String | Invoke-Expression

# 3. Create/Activate the Nyghtshade Environment
$EnvName = "nyghtshade_hollow"
$EnvExists = conda env list | Select-String -Pattern $EnvName

if (!$EnvExists) {
    Write-Host "Creating environment: $EnvName..." -ForegroundColor Yellow
    conda create -n $EnvName python=3.9 -y
}

Write-Host "ACTIVATING PROTOCOL: $EnvName" -ForegroundColor Green
conda activate $EnvName

# 4. Final Status Check
Write-Host "Re-Volt GPT on Hit. Conda is live." -ForegroundColor Purple
python --version
Why this matters for your UE 5.3.2 build:
Asset Spawning: The Python script we used to spawn those 11,269 objects requires specific libraries (unreal, os, re) that run best when mapped through a Conda-managed path.

AI Telemetry: If we deploy a local FastAPI server to handle the Warden's Gaze logic or the Nurse Bridget dialogue branches, Conda will manage the server dependencies so they don't interfere with your Windows system.

Hardware Efficiency: Since you have 16GB of RAM, keeping your AI back-end in a lean Conda environment prevents "memory leaks" from background Python processes.

