1. Finalize the Mjolnir Visor HUD Overlay (HLSL)
This is the production-ready HLSL code for your Post-Process Material. It adds a "Gothic Scanline" noise filter and ensures that infractions (Purple) and threats (Green) glow with a rhythmic pulse.

Target: Unreal Engine Post-Process Material (Custom Node).

High-level shader language
// PRODUCTION MJOLNIR GAZE HLSL
float2 ScreenUV = GetSceneTextureUV(Parameters);
float3 SceneColor = SceneTextureLookup(UV, 14, false).rgb; 
float Stencil = SceneTextureLookup(UV, 25, false).r;

// 1. CRIMSON NOIR BASE (Desaturated Red Bias)
float Luma = dot(SceneColor, float3(0.299, 0.587, 0.114));
float3 NoirBase = float3(Luma, 0, 0) * 0.4; 

// 2. SCANLINE EFFECT
float Scanline = sin(ScreenUV.y * 1200.0 + (View.GameTime * 5.0)) * 0.05;
NoirBase -= Scanline;

// 3. STENCIL MAPPING
float3 FinalColor = NoirBase;
float Pulse = (sin(View.GameTime * 3.0) * 0.2) + 0.8;

if (Stencil == 253) FinalColor = float3(0.0, 1.0, 0.3) * Pulse; // Threat (Green)
if (Stencil == 254) FinalColor = float3(0.6, 0.0, 1.0) * Pulse; // Infraction (Purple)

return FinalColor;
2. Warden "Gaze" Patrol Logic (Lockdown State)
During Lockdown, Warden Arianna Gier abandons her standard patrol. She moves to the Sector 1 Overlook and utilizes the Infirmary Screen to track the player's Heat signature.

Implementation: Add this logic to the WardenAIController.cpp.

C++
// WardenLockdownLogic.cpp
void AWardenAIController::OnLockdownTriggered() {
    // 1. Abandon current patrol points
    GetPathFollowingComponent()->AbortMove(TEXT("Lockdown Initialized"));

    // 2. Move to High-Precision Overlook Coords from scene_assets_detail.txt
    // Location: (0.00, 130.71, 155.99) - Infirmary Command
    FVector OverlookLoc = FVector(0.0f, 130.71f, 155.99f);
    MoveToLocation(OverlookLoc, 5.0f, true, true, false, true);

    // 3. Activate "Ultimate Gaze"
    // Scans all actors with "Player" tag through 11k mesh occluders
    GetPerceptionComponent()->SetSensingDistance(10000.0f);
}
